    -- One unique short string per room (44 total), shown on A-press.
    -- BANKED (bank 1): the ~81 string literals + switch code are ~2.5 KB;
    -- resident they overflow the 16 KB GB home bank past 0x4000, where the
    -- linker SILENTLY overlaps them with the banked MAPS data = a runtime
    -- crash (LCD off). bank(1) far-calls switch + restore around the call, so
    -- the data-seam SWITCH_ROM interplay is safe. Ignored on the Lynx/PCE.
    bank(1) function sign_text(id: u8, c: u8, r: u8) {
